  {
   "seq": 1,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "A key aim of Services in Kubernetes is that you don't need to modify your existing\napplication to use an unfamiliar service discovery mechanism.\nYou can run code in Pods, whether this is a code designed for a cloud-native world, or\nan older app you've containerized. You use a Service to make that set of Pods available\non the network so that clients can interact with it.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 0,
   "target": "Kubernetes 中服务的一个关键目标是：您无需修改现有应用，即可使用不熟悉的服务发现机制。\n您可以在 Pod 中运行代码，无论这些代码是为云原生环境设计的，还是已经容器化的旧版应用。您可以使用服务让这组 Pod 在网络上可用，以便客户端与其交互。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 92,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Pods",
     "target": "Pod",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Service",
     "target": "服务",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Kubernetes",
     "target": "Kubernetes",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Services",
     "target": "服务",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "service discovery",
     "target": "服务发现",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "seq": 2,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "If you use a Deployment to run your app,\nthat Deployment can create and destroy Pods dynamically. From one moment to the next,\nyou don't know how many of those Pods are working and healthy; you might not even know\nwhat those healthy Pods are named.\nKubernetes Pods are created and destroyed\nto match the desired state of your cluster. Pods are ephemeral resources (you should not\nexpect that an individual Pod is reliable and durable).",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 0,
   "target": "如果您使用 Deployment 运行应用，该 Deployment 可以动态创建和销毁 Pod。从一个时刻到下一个时刻，您不知道有多少个 Pod 正在工作并处于健康状态；您甚至可能不知道这些健康 Pod 的名称。\nKubernetes 会创建和销毁 Pod，以匹配集群的期望状态。Pod 是临时资源（您不应认为单个 Pod 是可靠且持久的）。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 92,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Pods",
     "target": "Pod",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Kubernetes",
     "target": "Kubernetes",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Deployment",
     "target": "Deployment",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Pod",
     "target": "Pod",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "seq": 3,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "Each Pod gets its own IP address (Kubernetes expects network plugins to ensure this).\nFor a given Deployment in your cluster, the set of Pods running in one moment in\ntime could be different from the set of Pods running that application a moment later.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 0,
   "target": "每个 Pod 都会获得自己的 IP 地址（Kubernetes 要求网络插件确保这一点）。\n对于集群中的某个 Deployment，在某一时刻运行的 Pod 集合，可能不同于片刻之后运行该应用的 Pod 集合。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 92,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Pods",
     "target": "Pod",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Kubernetes",
     "target": "Kubernetes",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Deployment",
     "target": "Deployment",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Pod",
     "target": "Pod",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "IP address",
     "target": "IP 地址",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "seq": 4,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "This leads to a problem: if some set of Pods (call them \"backends\") provides\nfunctionality to other Pods (call them \"frontends\") inside your cluster,\nhow do the frontends find out and keep track of which IP address to connect\nto, so that the frontend can use the backend part of the workload?",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 0,
   "target": "这会引发一个问题：如果某组 Pod（称为“后端”）向集群内的其他 Pod（称为“前端”）提供功能，那么前端如何发现并持续跟踪应连接的 IP 地址，从而使用工作负载中的后端部分？",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 92,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Pods",
     "target": "Pod",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "frontends",
     "target": "前端",
