  {
   "seq": 7,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "The Service API, part of Kubernetes, is an abstraction to help you expose groups of\nPods over a network. Each Service object defines a logical set of endpoints (usually\nthese endpoints are Pods) along with a policy about how to make those pods accessible.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "服务 API 是 Kubernetes 的一部分，是一种抽象，用于帮助你通过网络公开 Pod 组。每个服务对象都会定义一组逻辑端点（通常这些端点是 Pod），以及如何使这些 Pod 可访问的策略。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 99,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Pods",
     "target": "Pod",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Service",
     "target": "服务",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Kubernetes",
     "target": "Kubernetes",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "endpoints",
     "target": "端点",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "seq": 8,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "For example, consider a stateless image-processing backend which is running with\n3 replicas.  Those replicas are fungible&mdash;frontends do not care which backend\nthey use.  While the actual Pods that compose the backend set may change, the\nfrontend clients should not need to be aware of that, nor should they need to keep\ntrack of the set of backends themselves.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "例如，考虑一个运行着 3 个副本的无状态图像处理后端。这些副本是可互换的&mdash;前端并不关心使用哪个后端。虽然组成后端集合的实际 Pod 可能会发生变化，但前端客户端不应需要了解这些变化，也不应需要自行跟踪后端集合。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 99,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Pods",
     "target": "Pod",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "frontends",
     "target": "前端",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "backends",
     "target": "后端",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "replicas",
     "target": "副本",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "seq": 9,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "The Service abstraction enables this decoupling.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "服务抽象实现了这种解耦。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 99,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Service",
     "target": "服务",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "seq": 10,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "Canary deployments are a common use case for Services. To learn what's involved, follow the [Deploy a Release Using a Canary Deployment](/docs/tutorials/stateless-application/canary-deployment/) tutorial.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "金丝雀部署是服务的常见使用场景。要了解其中涉及的内容，请参阅[使用金丝雀 Deployment 发布版本](/docs/tutorials/stateless-application/canary-deployment/)教程。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 99,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Services",
     "target": "服务",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Deployment",
     "target": "Deployment",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "seq": 11,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "The set of Pods targeted by a Service is usually determined\nby a selector that you\ndefine.\nTo learn about other ways to define Service endpoints,\nsee [Services _without_ selectors](#services-without-selectors).",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "服务所针对的 Pod 集合通常由你定义的选择器确定。\n要了解定义服务端点的其他方式，请参阅[不使用选择器的服务](#services-without-selectors)。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 99,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Pods",
     "target": "Pod",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Service",
     "target": "服务",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Services",
     "target": "服务",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "endpoints",
     "target": "端点",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "seq": 12,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "If your workload speaks HTTP, you might choose to use an\n[Ingress](/docs/concepts/services-networking/ingress/) to control how web traffic\nreaches that workload.\nIngress is not a Service type, but it acts as the entry point for your\ncluster. An Ingress lets you consolidate your routing rules into a single resource, so\nthat you can expose multiple components of your workload, running separately in your\ncluster, behind a single listener.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "如果你的工作负载使用 HTTP，则可以选择使用[Ingress](/docs/concepts/services-networking/ingress/)来控制 Web 流量如何到达该工作负载。\nIngress 不是一种服务类型，但它充当集群的入口点。Ingress 允许你将路由规则整合到单个资源中，这样，你就可以通过单个侦听器公开工作负载的多个组件，而这些组件在集群中分别运行。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 99,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "Service",
     "target": "服务",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Ingress",
     "target": "Ingress",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false
  },
  {
   "seq": 13,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "The [Gateway](https://gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io/#what-is-the-gateway-api) API for Kubernetes\nprovides extra capabilities beyond Ingress and Service. You can add Gateway to your cluster -\nit is a family of extension APIs, implemented using\nCustomResourceDefinitions -\nand then use these to configure access to network services that are running in your cluster.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "Kubernetes 的 [Gateway](https://gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io/#what-is-the-gateway-api) API 提供了超越 Ingress 和服务的额外功能。你可以将 Gateway 添加到集群中——它是一组扩展 API，使用自定义资源定义实现——然后使用这些 API 配置对集群中运行的网络服务的访问。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": 99,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
